{"id":"coding-conditions","title":"Coding: making decisions with if and else","subject":"Coding","label":"Coding","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":158,"duration":158.24,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":440,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"The puzzle","start":0,"end":12.655},{"id":"explain","title":"Conditions","start":12.655,"end":49.425},{"id":"explain2","title":"Combining","start":49.425,"end":69.945},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":69.945,"end":96.805},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":96.805,"end":109.755},{"id":"answer","title":"The answer","start":109.755,"end":116.215},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Watch out","start":116.215,"end":133.385},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":133.385,"end":158.24}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":6.65,"text":"Think about this. A game shows your score and decides, all by itself, whether you passed or you failed.","w":[0.52,0.76,0.98,1.8,1.9,2.22,2.46,2.62,2.98,3.08,4.04,4.24,4.44,5.2,5.42,5.58,6.1,6.18,6.32]},{"s":0,"a":6.95,"b":12.23,"text":"How does it know? I'm Kora, and in the next three minutes you'll learn how code makes decisions.","w":[7.02,7.22,7.4,7.48,8.28,8.46,9.24,9.36,9.44,9.6,9.88,10.14,10.44,10.68,10.92,11.14,11.4,11.62]},{"s":1,"a":13.08,"b":18.54,"text":"At the heart of every decision is a condition. A condition is simply a question with a yes or no answer.","w":[13.16,13.26,13.4,13.62,13.82,14.02,14.44,14.56,14.62,15.68,15.78,16.24,16.38,16.72,16.8,17.18,17.34,17.44,17.84,18,18.22]},{"s":1,"a":18.84,"b":23.02,"text":"In code, that answer is a boolean, written as True or False.","w":[18.92,19.1,19.8,20.08,20.44,20.56,20.62,21.26,21.68,21.9,22.36,22.52]},{"s":1,"a":23.32,"b":28.06,"text":"To ask the question, you compare things. Equal to uses two equals signs.","w":[23.34,23.54,23.76,23.86,24.26,24.42,24.74,25.5,25.82,26.54,26.9,27.24,27.56]},{"s":1,"a":28.36,"b":35.85,"text":"Not equal to, greater than, less than, greater than or equal to, and less than or equal to all work as they sound.","w":[28.46,28.76,29.06,29.82,30.16,30.84,31.08,31.72,32.04,32.38,32.56,32.82,33.48,33.66,33.94,34.26,34.42,34.68,34.86,35.02,35.26,35.36,35.52]},{"s":1,"a":36.15,"b":40.82,"text":"Then comes the if statement. It runs its block of code only when the condition is True.","w":[36.22,36.54,36.84,37,37.12,38.1,38.22,38.54,38.68,38.98,39.1,39.48,39.68,39.82,39.94,40.36,40.48]},{"s":1,"a":41.12,"b":46,"text":"Else gives the other path. Elif, short for else if, checks another condition.","w":[41.2,41.5,41.72,41.92,42.14,42.98,43.58,43.86,44.08,44.38,44.88,45.22,45.52]},{"s":1,"a":46.3,"b":49,"text":"The first one that is True wins, top to bottom.","w":[46.3,46.46,46.86,47,47.16,47.34,47.6,48.24,48.5,48.62]},{"s":2,"a":49.85,"b":54.98,"text":"Two more things. And, or and not combine conditions. And needs both sides true.","w":[49.86,50.06,50.26,51.1,51.66,51.84,51.98,52.22,52.66,53.5,53.62,53.92,54.18,54.62]},{"s":2,"a":55.28,"b":59.81,"text":"Or needs at least one. Not flips true to false, and false to true.","w":[55.32,55.48,55.82,55.92,56.32,57.1,57.36,57.72,57.94,58.08,58.96,59.14,59.4,59.54]},{"s":2,"a":60.11,"b":64.84,"text":"In Python, the block is shown by indentation, a few spaces at the start of each line.","w":[60.16,60.32,60.88,61.02,61.34,61.44,61.74,61.96,63.04,63.12,63.34,63.76,63.84,63.96,64.2,64.3,64.5]},{"s":2,"a":65.14,"b":69.52,"text":"Those spaces are not decoration. They tell Python what belongs to the if.","w":[65.18,65.42,65.88,66.06,66.32,67.42,67.6,67.86,68.44,68.64,69.12,69.24,69.42]},{"s":3,"a":70.37,"b":73.82,"text":"Let's work one through. Suppose score equals sixty-two.","w":[70.37,70.74,71.05,71.29,71.85,72.34,72.71,73.14]},{"s":3,"a":74.12,"b":80.04,"text":"The code says: if score is greater than or equal to fifty, print pass. Else, print try again.","w":[74.14,74.3,74.56,75.26,75.44,75.82,75.96,76.3,76.48,76.62,76.9,77.04,77.86,78.2,78.8,79.04,79.42,79.72]},{"s":3,"a":80.34,"b":85.03,"text":"Sixty-two is greater than fifty, so the condition is True, and it prints pass.","w":[80.34,80.93,81.11,81.59,81.88,82.3,82.48,82.71,83.31,83.49,83.84,84.08,84.26,84.67]},{"s":3,"a":85.33,"b":91.67,"text":"Now a grade ladder. Seventy or more is A. Fifty or more is pass. Else, fail.","w":[85.46,85.9,86.02,86.38,87.2,87.58,87.72,88.1,88.34,89.04,89.38,89.48,89.7,89.84,90.76,91.32]},{"s":3,"a":91.97,"b":96.38,"text":"With sixty-two, it skips the first check, the second is True, so it prints pass.","w":[91.97,92.24,92.84,93,93.33,93.55,93.88,94.26,94.47,94.86,95.02,95.35,95.51,95.67,96.05]},{"s":4,"a":97.23,"b":99.69,"text":"Quick check. Age equals fifteen.","w":[97.28,97.52,98.42,98.78,99.14]},{"s":4,"a":99.99,"b":105.77,"text":"The code says: if age is greater than or equal to eighteen, print adult. Else, print minor.","w":[100,100.16,100.46,101.22,101.46,101.66,101.8,102.1,102.26,102.4,102.64,102.8,103.66,104,104.78,105.16,105.42]},{"s":4,"a":106.07,"b":106.87,"text":"What is printed?","w":[106.12,106.3,106.44]},{"s":4,"a":107.32,"b":109.33,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[107.34,107.68,107.94,108.06,108.34,108.8,108.98]},{"s":5,"a":110.18,"b":115.79,"text":"It prints minor. Fifteen is less than eighteen, so the condition is False, and else takes over.","w":[110.24,110.38,110.72,111.62,112.14,112.28,112.5,112.66,113.34,113.48,113.6,114.06,114.18,114.88,115.06,115.26,115.54]},{"s":6,"a":116.64,"b":123.78,"text":"Three things to watch. First, one equals sign assigns a value. Two equals signs compare. Use two.","w":[116.7,116.98,117.28,117.4,118.28,118.78,119.04,119.4,119.86,120.32,120.4,121.36,121.64,122,122.36,123.26,123.46]},{"s":6,"a":124.08,"b":129.47,"text":"Second, order matters in a ladder. Put the strictest check first, or a later one can never run.","w":[124.2,124.72,125,125.44,125.56,125.64,126.36,126.56,126.68,127.16,127.44,128.08,128.22,128.3,128.66,128.8,128.98,129.24]},{"s":6,"a":129.77,"b":132.96,"text":"Third, don't forget the indentation, or your block won't work.","w":[129.8,130.32,130.56,130.88,131,131.94,132.06,132.22,132.52,132.74]},{"s":7,"a":133.81,"b":138.35,"text":"So, three points. A condition is a yes or no question, a boolean.","w":[133.94,134.64,134.9,135.7,135.76,136.26,136.38,136.46,136.72,136.82,137,137.8,137.88]},{"s":7,"a":138.65,"b":143.13,"text":"If runs its block when the condition is True; else and elif handle the rest.","w":[138.7,138.88,139.16,139.32,139.74,139.9,140.02,140.44,140.58,141.36,141.82,142.02,142.36,142.66,142.78]},{"s":7,"a":143.43,"b":147.18,"text":"And, or and not combine conditions, and indentation marks the block.","w":[143.5,143.78,144.08,144.2,144.4,144.78,145.66,145.84,146.52,146.82,146.92]},{"s":7,"a":147.48,"b":152.63,"text":"Top tip: read your ladder from the top and ask, could any check below ever be reached?","w":[147.54,147.86,148.56,148.78,148.94,149.24,149.4,149.52,149.88,150.06,150.64,150.92,151.16,151.44,151.88,152.06,152.22]},{"s":7,"a":153.08,"b":157.64,"text":"Well done. This is Kora at Knowzone, and I'll see you in the next lesson.","w":[153.14,153.42,154.32,154.52,154.68,155.14,155.28,156.18,156.32,156.52,156.68,156.84,156.92,157.04,157.26]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Decision puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Game decides pass/fail from score"},{"at":6.85,"kind":"text","text":"Code makes decisions"}]},{"at":12.83,"heading":"Conditions & booleans","items":[{"at":12.98,"kind":"term","text":"Condition","detail":"A question with a yes or no answer"},{"at":18.74,"kind":"term","text":"Boolean","detail":"True or False answer in code"},{"at":23.22,"kind":"formula","text":"== equal to"},{"at":28.26,"kind":"text","text":"Comparisons: != > < >= <="}]},{"at":35.9,"heading":"if, else, elif","items":[{"at":36.05,"kind":"term","text":"if","detail":"Runs its block only when condition is True"},{"at":41.02,"kind":"term","text":"else / elif","detail":"Other path; elif checks another condition"},{"at":46.2,"kind":"text","text":"First True condition wins, top to bottom"}]},{"at":49.6,"heading":"Combining conditions","items":[{"at":49.75,"kind":"term","text":"and / or / not","detail":"Combine conditions; and: both true"},{"at":55.18,"kind":"term","text":"or / not","detail":"or: at least one true; not: flips true to false"},{"at":60.01,"kind":"term","text":"Indentation","detail":"A few spaces at the start of each line"},{"at":65.04,"kind":"text","text":"Spaces show what belongs to the if"}]},{"at":70.12,"heading":"Worked example: pass","items":[{"at":70.27,"kind":"formula","text":"score = 62"},{"at":74.02,"kind":"formula","text":"if score >= 50: print(\"pass\")"},{"at":74.02,"kind":"formula","text":"else: print(\"try again\")"},{"at":80.24,"kind":"step","text":"62 >= 50 is True"},{"at":80.24,"kind":"text","text":"True → prints pass"}]},{"at":85.08,"heading":"Worked example: ladder","items":[{"at":85.23,"kind":"text","text":"score >= 70: A; score >= 50: pass; else: fail"},{"at":91.87,"kind":"step","text":"62 < 70"},{"at":91.87,"kind":"step","text":"62 >= 50 is True"},{"at":91.87,"kind":"text","text":"second True → prints pass"}]},{"at":96.81,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":96.81,"kind":"question","text":"age = 15. if age >= 18: print(\"adult\") else: print(\"minor\"). What is printed?"}]},{"at":109.93,"heading":"Answer: minor","items":[{"at":110.08,"kind":"text","text":"prints minor"},{"at":110.08,"kind":"text","text":"15 < 18 → False; else runs"}]},{"at":116.39,"heading":"Watch out","items":[{"at":116.54,"kind":"wrong","text":"Using = when you mean to compare"},{"at":116.54,"kind":"right","text":"= assigns a value; == compares"},{"at":123.98,"kind":"wrong","text":"Ladder order: loose check first"},{"at":129.67,"kind":"wrong","text":"Forget indentation"}]},{"at":133.56,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":133.71,"kind":"text","text":"Condition = yes/no question; boolean"},{"at":138.55,"kind":"text","text":"if True runs block; else/elif handle rest"},{"at":143.33,"kind":"text","text":"and, or, not combine; indentation marks block"},{"at":147.38,"kind":"tip","text":"Read ladder top-down: could any check below be reached?"}]}],"check":{"at":109.58,"seconds":10,"question":"age = 15. if age >= 18: print(\"adult\") else: print(\"minor\"). What is printed?","answer":"minor. 15 >= 18 is False, so the else branch runs."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}